{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Catch-Up Subscription.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Catch-Up Subscription.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"catch up subscription catch up subscription","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Catch-Up Subscription.md","fileName":"Catch-Up Subscription.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Catch-Up Subscription","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 20:53\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Event Sourcing and Projections]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Event Sourcing and Projections","Projection Checkpoint","Projection","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Catch-Up Subscription.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Catch-Up Subscription.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"catch up subscription catch up subscription","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Catch-Up Subscription.md","fileName":"Catch-Up Subscription.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Catch-Up Subscription","heading":"Catch-Up Subscription","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A catch-up subscription reads an event stream from a stored [[Projection Checkpoint]], processes historical events until it reaches the stream's end, and then continues with new events in real time. Starting from the beginning allows a new [[Projection]] to build a read model for a system that already has a long history. Resetting the checkpoint and deleting the read model triggers a rebuild, so the event history remains the authoritative input.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Event Sourcing and Projections","Projection Checkpoint","Projection","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Catch-Up Subscription.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Catch-Up Subscription.md","sourceT